column271:
13/Feb/26 1:35 PM;mmyles;Initial evaluation indicates that the vast majority of CAB FQT requirements should be able to be verified by design review. The requirements we had allocated to ELCH should be re-allocated to ENVR or INSP/DRVW. Most of the INSP requirements can likely be DRVW'd. I set up a meeting for 2/18 to discuss this further with the wider PHC team. Of the remaining few requirements that we would want to test I think we should be able to do these on the build 1 (non-tactical structure) EDMs. With this plan we would do CAB FQT, RTR FQT, and SQT on build 1 EDMs and EQT on build 2 EDMs. 

I believe the lighting equipment requirements can be DRVW'd (physical mounting and internal wiring) or EQT'd (power). We will also perform some validation testing of the lighting equipment at SQT. We should not need the lighting equipment for CAB FQT if these assumptions hold.

Need to update IMS for this approach.;;;

